---
description: Lumen project rules for Cursor's agent
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before making changes and follow it. It has the architecture
(AMD box runs the brain and models, the Mac runs `scripts/jupyter_bridge.py` + cloudflared), the page map
(`/captions` is the one wearer page; `/headset` redirects there), the Databricks paths and the known gaps.
The short version:

- Never push to `main`. Draft PR while working, mark Ready when done; the auto-merge robot merges when CI is green.
  From Sun Oct 11, 8:00 AM ET only PRs labeled `hotfix` merge.
- Before saying you're done, run `cd server && python -m pytest -q` and `cd web && npm run build`.
- The alert JSON in `docs/agent-line.md` is a contract; don't change it unless asked.
- No LLM decides whether a safety alert fires. No face recognition. No live video leaves a phone.
- Sound direction: headset is the center, back cam is behind, security phone is on the chest (`server/app/direction.py`). SAID and PSELDNets are the reference models. Do not stack those phone streams into their checkpoints. Direction never fires an alert.
- Captions and alerts stay large, plain and high contrast. Black/gray/white design; the Eclipse logo is the only color.
- Never use `sudo` or reinstall `torch` on the AMD box. Never commit tokens or API keys.
- Keep changes small and explain them in plain words.
